Make man work in w64devkit: find pages in <bindir>/../share/man after
$MANPATH, format them with the kit's nroff next to busybox.exe (still
overridable with DEFINE nroff), and page with less -R. Pass -Tutf8 only
when the ANSI code page is UTF-8. When stdout is not a terminal, write
the formatter's plain output directly instead of piping through col,
which does not exist, and copy cat pages as they are.

Run the formatter in the manpath element, or in the user's directory for
an explicit path, so that .so requests in page bodies resolve. Look up
x86_64-w64-mingw32-NAME and i686-w64-mingw32-NAME as NAME when there is
no page under the full name. Accept backslashes in absolute paths, and
CRLF in .so stubs. Append $MANROFFOPT to the formatter options, as
man-db does, so that, e.g., MANROFFOPT=-dAD=l sets pages ragged-right.

